  "query_preview": ".. Tuesday and Wednesday feature the best chances for \nwidespread rain and storms as potent trough deepens over the \nHudson Bay and cold front digs south during peak heating. Cursory\nglance shows decent instability in proximity to the front\ncoinciding with 30+ knots of bulk shear, which would suggest the\npossibility of strong storms developing Tuesday afternoon. ML\nguidance, and thus SPC outlook, show the main severe threat off \nto our southwest, though trends have been shifting northward. WPC\nERO likewise highlights areas along/south of Hwy 29 in a Day 4 \nslight risk for excessive rainfall due to skinny CAPE profiles and\npotential for backbuilding storms. Regardless, will bear watching\nas details come into focus in the next couple of days. Cooler and\nmore stable air then filters in behind the front on Wednesday, \nwith temperatures settling mainly in the 70s. Highs should read \nnear normal through most of next week.",
